    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for perl-DBI",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for perl-DBI fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-78030: arbitrary modules loaded due to unvalidated `dbm_type` and `dbm_mldbm` attributes in `DBD::DBM`\n  (bsc#1281704).\n- CVE-2026-88815: numeric value incorrectly treated as strings in `sql_type_cast_svpv` allows for process crash\n  (bsc#1283055).\n- CVE-2026-88816: numeric value incorrectly treated as strings in `FetchHashKeyName` allows for process crash\n  (bsc#1283056).\n- CVE-2026-108518: type confusion in `dbi_profile` when a database handle is destroyed under a Profile Path with an\n  `{attr}` element can lead to crash (bsc#1286552).\n- CVE-2026-111879: later open of a `DBD::DBM table` can hang due to failed `open_data` not releasing the table's lock\n  (bsc#1286553).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
